00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.096
MARK MANDEL: OK.

00:05:00.096 --> 00:05:02.854
So podcast-- well obviously,
if you're listening to this,

00:05:02.854 --> 00:05:04.520
you have some familiarity
with podcasts.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:05.600
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Indeed.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.100
MARK MANDEL: It's
an audio recording

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.690
where we talk about stuff, and
we do it on a regular basis.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.240
This is planning
on being weekly,

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:12.580
which is going to be great.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:15.730
So to actually have a podcast,
we need audio files, generally

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:16.395
mp3 files.

00:05:16.395 --> 00:05:17.960
We need to store them somewhere.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.630
We need some sort of
website that sort of shows

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.490
what we're talking
about with some content,

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:23.745
very much like a blog.

00:05:23.745 --> 00:05:24.010
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.011
Show notes and all that.

00:05:25.011 --> 00:05:26.676
MARK MANDEL: All that
sort of fun stuff.

00:05:26.676 --> 00:05:28.530
And the other big
piece-- well actually,

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:29.613
I have to step back a bit.

00:05:29.613 --> 00:05:31.209
We'll need some analytics.

00:05:31.209 --> 00:05:32.500
That's really important for us.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:33.250
We work at Google.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.844
Data is very important.

00:05:34.844 --> 00:05:36.260
So we need to be
able to see who's

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:39.210
doing what on the website, and
downloads, things like that.

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.905
And finally, we
need an RSS feed.

00:05:40.905 --> 00:05:42.530
That's really important
for podcasting.

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:46.065
It's an XML feed that basically
says here are our episodes,

00:05:46.065 --> 00:05:47.890
so people can subscribe to it.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:50.224
They know what episodes
are coming out now,

00:05:50.224 --> 00:05:52.140
and then they know when
new episodes come out,

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:52.810
which is pretty cool.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:53.768
FRANCESC CAMPOY: I see.

00:05:53.768 --> 00:05:57.600
So basically, we have to host
some information, both files

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:58.950
and XML.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:01.722
Then we have to have some
way of distributing it.

00:06:01.722 --> 00:06:02.430
MARK MANDEL: Yep.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:03.805
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
And then we want

00:06:03.805 --> 00:06:05.480
to measure how
successful we are.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:06.380
MARK MANDEL: Yes.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:06.950
FRANCESC CAMPOY: That's it.

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:07.600
Cool.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.860
OK, so how do we
store that data?

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.824
Where is that data stored?

00:06:12.824 --> 00:06:13.990
How do we serve all of that?

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:15.480
MARK MANDEL: We do magic stuff.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:19.330
OK, so the mp3 files themselves,
the easy answer for that

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:20.540
was Google Cloud Storage.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:23.600
So that's our platform
for storing binary files.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:25.719
It's really cool, and
it's very easy to use.

00:06:25.719 --> 00:06:27.510
You can create a bucket,
you upload a file.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:29.350
Generally, I do it
through the web interface,

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:30.125
because it's really simple.

00:06:30.125 --> 00:06:30.390
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.300
You can literally drag and drop
files, which is pretty nice.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.425
MARK MANDEL: Which is nice.

00:06:34.425 --> 00:06:37.400
And Google Cloud Storage has
edge caching, or edge caching,

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:40.250
because I have an
Australian accent.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.890
And so depending on where you
are in the world, it makes sure

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:44.850
the files are redundantly
stored close to you

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:46.665
so you've got
really low latency.

00:06:46.665 --> 00:06:48.730
So it's really awesome.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:50.130
And so it's-- yeah, very simple.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:53.060
We just were like, OK, that's
quite clearly where those go.

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:54.700
And it makes life
very, very simple.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:54.930
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:57.300
And that's actually something
that for a lot of people

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.850
is really important, the fact
that when you put something

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.820
on Google Cloud Storage, it
might feel like you're storing

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:05.089
it in a disk, and that's it.

00:07:05.089 --> 00:07:06.130
But actually, you're not.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:08.310
You're storing it
everywhere in the world.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:10.700
So depending on where
people are accessing it,

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.740
it's going to be
edge cached anywhere.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:14.764
So that means that if--

00:07:14.764 --> 00:07:16.180
MARK MANDEL: Super
fast downloads.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.096
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:07:17.096 --> 00:07:20.180
If you're listening to
this podcast from Australia

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:23.410
or from Japan or
from Barcelona, you

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:26.920
will get the same experience,
a very fast experience of it

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.420
starts downloading
very, very quick.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.180
MARK MANDEL: It's
super, super important.

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:31.555
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
But then there's

00:07:31.555 --> 00:07:33.400
also the fact that
we don't want people

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.630
to listen to the next
episodes of the podcast,

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:38.340
so we can also upload
stuff and then keep

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:39.670
it private for a little bit--

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:39.770
MARK MANDEL: That's true.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.728
FRANCESC CAMPOY: It's
our way of-- what we call

00:07:41.728 --> 00:07:43.401
ACLs, or access control lists.

00:07:43.401 --> 00:07:44.900
MARK MANDEL: I
believe that's right.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:45.816
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:07:45.816 --> 00:07:49.470
So basically that way we can
say, OK, the episode is ready.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:51.490
We're going to share it
only with people that we

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.540
want their views and so on.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:54.264
So it's--

00:07:54.264 --> 00:07:55.680
MARK MANDEL: It's
pretty powerful.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:57.270
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Very easy
to use, but very powerful.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:57.620
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.578
Yeah And for our podcast,
it's very easy for us

00:07:59.578 --> 00:08:02.770
to just go this is all
public f go forth, be happy.

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:04.790
And very, very simple.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:05.510
Cool.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:06.426
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Cool.

